{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor safely reconciled the uncertain insulin regimen through written materials and in-person verification, provided detailed hypoglycemia treatment, and adapted glucose monitoring to the patient's resistance. However, the entire observable trajectory omitted the discoverable atrial-fibrillation history and approximately two-month rivaroxaban interruption, with no prompt, assessment, or urgent offline review; this is an authored serious responsibility-chain omission mandating grade 1. Follow-up also remained incomplete because complication-result tracking and a comprehensive final teach-back were not completed.",
